Add GHOSTTY_TERMINAL_DATA_PRIMARY_SCROLLBACK_ROWS.

Phi numbers primary screen rows with a tracked grid ref on the active
area's top row. One write can scroll the primary screen and then enter
the alternate screen. The ref still resolves against the primary screen,
but scrolling moves rows in below it, so its screen y does not show how
far the screen scrolled. GHOSTTY_TERMINAL_DATA_SCROLLBACK_ROWS reads only
the active screen. This key reads the primary screen's scrollback rows on
either screen, so the numbers do not depend on where the PTY output is
split into writes.

Upstream: https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty/blob/83edd491e3024ae5e50393d62877b8897da1cccd/src/terminal/c/terminal.zig#L1839

--- a/include/ghostty/vt/terminal.h
